layout: layouts/feature.njk
wide: true
title: Microfrontend | Shellui
description: Microfrontend support in Shellui - layout modes, navigation, and shared shell chrome.
eyebrow: Features
heading: Microfrontend
lede: The runtime that stitches your apps together. Sidebar navigation, layout modes, modals, drawers, themes, and i18n - all configured from a single shell.
---

<div class="prose max-w-2xl">
  <p>Shellui owns the shell around your app: sidebar navigation, layout modes, modals, drawers, and how microfrontends render inside the chrome. Apps keep their own UI. The shell keeps the shared surface consistent.</p>
</div>

<div class="mt-14 grid items-center gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(16rem,22rem)] lg:gap-14">
  <div class="max-w-xl">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl dark:text-white">Layout modes</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Switch between a colored sidebar, a top bar, and a windowed desktop from one config. Every microfrontend inherits the chrome, so navigation and the app canvas stay aligned when the layout changes.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-md lg:mx-0 lg:max-w-none">
    {% include "shell-layout-anim.njk" %}
  </div>
</div>

<div class="mt-20">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl dark:text-white">Shared chrome</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Dialogs, toasts, modals, drawers, and settings live in the shell too. Hosted apps can open them without rebuilding overlays, and the markup stays in the page.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-10 grid gap-x-8 gap-y-12 sm:grid-cols-2">
    {% set chromes = [
      { type: "modal", blurb: "Open forms and detail views without leaving the current route." },
      { type: "dialog", blurb: "Short confirmations and choices, centered over the running app." },
      { type: "drawer", blurb: "Slide in side panels for details, lists, and secondary flows." },
      { type: "toast", blurb: "Transient status messages that appear without blocking the app." },
      { type: "settings", blurb: "Theme, language, and layout controls that apply across every microfrontend." }
    ] %}
    {% for item in chromes %}
      <div>
        {% set chrome = item.type %}
        {% include "shell-chrome-anim.njk" %}
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm/6 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">{{ item.blurb }}</p>
      </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</div>

<p class="mt-16 max-w-2xl text-base/7 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Next, see how <a class="font-medium text-primary-ink underline underline-offset-2 dark:text-primary" href="/features/authentication/">Authentication</a> handles sign-in, protected routes, and identity integration.</p>
